# testing
/coverage

# scripts and migrations are NOT ignored — both were, and it broke the repo.
#
# `package.json` wires every pipeline command to `scripts/*.mts`, and CLAUDE.md states that
# every schema change is a committed file in `migrations/`. With both directories ignored,
# a fresh clone could neither run `pnpm sync` nor rebuild the schema — and migration 0005
# had already been applied to the database while sitting untracked, which is the exact
# failure the migrations-only rule exists to prevent.

# claude code
.claude/settings.local.json
